# Documentation and Delivery

## Documentation Rules

- Keep `README.md` aligned with the actual state of the repository
- Update documentation when changing:
  - commands
  - environment variables
  - architecture
  - page structure
  - API behavior
  - security behavior
  - test strategy
- If a new rule becomes part of team workflow, document it in `.cursor/rules/` and reference it from `AGENTS.md` or `CLAUDE.md`

## Environment and Ops

- When adding a new env var, update `.env.example` and mention it in `README.md`
- When changing deploy or infrastructure behavior, update the relevant operational docs in the same change
- Do not leave hidden setup steps only in code comments or commit messages

## Delivery Checklist

- Read the target area before editing
- Keep the change focused and reversible
- Run the smallest relevant validation for the change
- Run broader validation when the blast radius is large
- Summarize assumptions if a decision was made without explicit user input

## Validation Expectations

- UI/component logic: run `bun run test:run` or a narrower equivalent if available
- Route or browser interaction changes: run `bun run test:e2e` when practical
- Broad code changes: run `bun run lint` and `bun run build`
- If validation is skipped, state why explicitly
